1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,266
I'm Peppa Pig. [snorts]

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:08,100
-This is my little brother, George.
-[snorts]

3
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:10,333
-This is Mommy Pig.
-[Mommy Pig snorts]

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,200
And this is Daddy Pig.

5
00:00:12,266 --> 00:00:14,200
-[Daddy Pig snorts]
-[all laugh]

6
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig. [snorts]

7
00:00:17,466 --> 00:00:19,766
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

8
00:00:21,133 --> 00:00:24,533
[narrator] Peppa and George are at Granny
and Grandpa Pig's house.

9
00:00:24,599 --> 00:00:26,266
[Peppa &amp; George giggling]

10
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:28,733
-[Peppa] Grandpa Pig!
-[George] Grandpa Ig!

11
00:00:28,799 --> 00:00:30,233
Oh, what's this?

12
00:00:30,299 --> 00:00:31,666
A cuckoo clock?

13
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:33,500
Yes, it goes:

14
00:00:33,566 --> 00:00:35,366
"Cuckoo, cuckoo!"

15
00:00:35,433 --> 00:00:37,199
But it's broken.

16
00:00:37,266 --> 00:00:40,333
[snorts] Can you mend it please,
Grandpa Pig?

17
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:41,433
Hmm. [snorts]

18
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,233
Let's take it to my shed.

19
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:47,733
[narrator] This is Grandpa Pig's shed,
where Grandpa mends things.

20
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,500
I'll take a look inside.

21
00:00:51,433 --> 00:00:52,666
Grandpa!

22
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:55,466
Now you've really broken it.

23
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:56,666
Oh.

24
00:00:56,733 --> 00:00:59,733
I wonder if I've got a book on clocks.

25
00:01:00,466 --> 00:01:02,099
Ah, here we are.

26
00:01:02,166 --> 00:01:04,366
How Clocks Work.

27
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:10,333
[narrator] Grandpa Pig has mended
the cuckoo clock.

28
00:01:10,399 --> 00:01:11,566
[Peppa &amp; George] Hooray!

29
00:01:12,633 --> 00:01:14,000
[bird cuckoos]

30
00:01:14,066 --> 00:01:15,133
[Peppa &amp; George giggle]

31
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,200
-[Peppa &amp; George cuckooing]
-[Grandpa Pig laughing]

32
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,466
[horn honks]

33
00:01:21,133 --> 00:01:24,100
[narrator] Mommy Pig has come
to pick up Peppa and George.

34
00:01:24,166 --> 00:01:28,200
[snorts] Mommy,
Grandpa's mended the cuckoo clock!

35
00:01:28,266 --> 00:01:29,466
That's nice. [snorts]

36
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:30,733
What's that?

37
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:32,600
It's my old computer.

38
00:01:32,666 --> 00:01:35,166
[snorts] I can't mend that.

39
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:36,233
It's not broken.

40
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,566
I've got a new computer.
I thought you might like my old one.

41
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:43,766
Um, I'm not sure I really need one.

42
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,699
Oh, a computer.

43
00:01:46,766 --> 00:01:47,733
What does it do?

44
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:50,033
You can do letters with it.

45
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,666
Look, Granny.

46
00:01:52,199 --> 00:01:55,466
[computer] A, B, C, D.

47
00:01:55,533 --> 00:01:56,533
And numbers.

48
00:01:57,166 --> 00:01:59,399
[computer] One, two, three.

49
00:01:59,466 --> 00:02:03,033
I'm afraid we might break it
by pressing the wrong button.

50
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:06,033
[chuckles] Don't worry.
You can't break it.

51
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:10,766
Just don't feed it milk
or biscuits or jelly.

52
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,633
[all laugh]

53
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:17,433
The best thing it does
is "Happy Mrs. Chicken."

54
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:18,400
[George snorts]

55
00:02:18,466 --> 00:02:21,700
When you press this button,
she lays an egg.

56
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:23,066
[chicken clucks &amp; farts]

57
00:02:23,133 --> 00:02:27,400
I am very good at it,
[snorts] but George is the best.

58
00:02:27,466 --> 00:02:30,066
-[George giggling]
-[chicken clucking and farting]

59
00:02:30,133 --> 00:02:31,400
[all laughing]

60
00:02:31,466 --> 00:02:33,033
That's fun.

61
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:38,066
Uh, perhaps, we should keep the computer,
Granny Pig.

62
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:42,366
-[grandparents] Goodbye.
-[Mommy Pig &amp; children] Bye-bye.

63
00:02:42,433 --> 00:02:43,600
[horn honks]

64
00:02:43,666 --> 00:02:47,766
Shall we do some work
on the computer, Granny Pig?

65
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,166
Yes, let's do some numbers and letters.

66
00:02:53,466 --> 00:02:56,066
[narrator] Peppa and her family
are having lunch.

67
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,666
I've given my old computer
to Granny and Grandpa.

68
00:02:59,733 --> 00:03:02,299
That's nice.
I wonder how they're getting on with it.

69
00:03:02,366 --> 00:03:04,066
[phone rings]

70
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,766
Hello, Peppa Pig speaking.

71
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:11,566
Uh, Peppa, I need to ask a question
about the computer.

72
00:03:11,633 --> 00:03:15,333
It's Grandpa.
He's broken the computer.

73
00:03:15,733 --> 00:03:18,733
What's the problem
with the computer, Grandpa Pig?

74
00:03:18,799 --> 00:03:21,399
-It's full of eggs.
-Eggs?

75
00:03:21,466 --> 00:03:25,200
Happy Mrs. Chicken won't lay
any more eggs.

76
00:03:25,266 --> 00:03:26,500
[computer beeps]

77
00:03:26,566 --> 00:03:28,066
[computer] I'm broken.

78
00:03:28,533 --> 00:03:30,433
Turn the computer off.

79
00:03:32,266 --> 00:03:33,799
Now turn it back on again.

80
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,200
Did that fix it?

81
00:03:36,266 --> 00:03:37,500
[computer beeping]

82
00:03:37,566 --> 00:03:40,233
[computer] I am very broken.

83
00:03:40,299 --> 00:03:42,100
That doesn't sound good.

84
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:43,766
Maybe it can't be mended.

85
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,466
We'll come round and pick it up.

86
00:03:45,533 --> 00:03:46,600
[computer beeping]

87
00:03:48,266 --> 00:03:51,166
Granny, we're here
to take the computer back.

88
00:03:51,233 --> 00:03:54,566
Oh. Grandpa Pig has taken it to his shed.

89
00:03:57,133 --> 00:03:59,200
There, that should do it.

90
00:04:00,133 --> 00:04:01,766
[computer] I am mended.

91
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,166
[Peppa &amp; George] Hooray!

92
00:04:03,233 --> 00:04:07,733
[snorts] My grandpa is the best
at mending things.

93
00:04:08,366 --> 00:04:10,066
Was it very hard to mend?

94
00:04:10,133 --> 00:04:11,700
Not at all.

95
00:04:11,766 --> 00:04:16,266
I found I had this book,
How Computers Work.

96
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:18,766
You don't want us to take it away now?

97
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,599
No. I need it for important work.

98
00:04:22,666 --> 00:04:24,666
For letter and number work?

99
00:04:24,733 --> 00:04:26,200
[snorts] No.

100
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:30,133
To beat Granny Pig's
"Happy Mrs. Chicken" score.

101
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:33,400
I laid 4020 eggs.

102
00:04:33,466 --> 00:04:34,433
[all] Wow.

103
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:39,166
So, I've got some work to do catching up.

104
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,566
[clucking and farting]

105
00:04:41,633 --> 00:04:43,633
[all laughing]

106
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:50,366
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

107
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,466
[narrator] Peppa, George and Danny
are having a day out

108
00:04:53,533 --> 00:04:55,366
on Granddad Dog's boat.

109
00:04:55,433 --> 00:04:59,000
[woofs] Can we go to Pirate Island today?

110
00:04:59,066 --> 00:05:00,066
Yes, Danny.

111
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:05,400
But first, we've got to deliver supplies
to my friend Grampy Rabbit.

112
00:05:05,466 --> 00:05:07,766
Where does Grampy Rabbit live?

113
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,566
-On a rock.
-On a rock?

114
00:05:10,633 --> 00:05:13,566
Yes. In that lighthouse.

115
00:05:13,633 --> 00:05:14,566
[children] Ooh.

116
00:05:14,633 --> 00:05:17,000
Ahoy there, matey.

117
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:19,066
I've brought your supplies.

118
00:05:19,133 --> 00:05:21,500
Oh. Thank you, Granddad Dog.

119
00:05:21,566 --> 00:05:23,800
I've got my crew with me today.

120
00:05:24,033 --> 00:05:26,200
Danny, Peppa and George.

121
00:05:26,266 --> 00:05:27,633
Visitors?

122
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:30,599
I haven't had visitors in many a moon.

123
00:05:31,266 --> 00:05:35,800
I get a bit lonely with just the sea
and sky for company.

124
00:05:36,533 --> 00:05:38,400
How long have you been here?

125
00:05:38,466 --> 00:05:40,166
-Since Tuesday.
-Oh.

126
00:05:40,233 --> 00:05:44,000
I've got tales to tell,
if you'd like to hear.

127
00:05:44,066 --> 00:05:46,066
-No, thanks.
-[children] Yes, please.

128
00:05:46,133 --> 00:05:49,700
Well, there's the sea and the sky, and--

129
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:52,333
I'm learning the banjo.
Would you like to hear a song?

130
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:54,700
-No, thanks.
-[children] Yes, please.

131
00:05:54,766 --> 00:05:57,133
♪ I got up this morning ♪

132
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,500
♪ The sea was still there ♪

133
00:05:59,566 --> 00:06:02,400
♪ So was the sky ♪

134
00:06:02,466 --> 00:06:04,433
♪ The sea, the sky, the sea, the sky ♪

135
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,166
[Granddad Dog] Here's your cheese.

136
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:09,599
-Oh. I've missed cheese.
-And a new book.

137
00:06:09,666 --> 00:06:11,599
How to Run a Lighthouse.

138
00:06:11,666 --> 00:06:13,366
Oh, that'll come in handy.

139
00:06:13,433 --> 00:06:16,099
Why is your house called a lighthouse?

140
00:06:16,166 --> 00:06:18,166
I'll show you, Peppa.

141
00:06:18,233 --> 00:06:20,700
[narrator] The staircase goes round
and round

142
00:06:20,766 --> 00:06:22,633
to the very top of the lighthouse.

143
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:26,000
[snorts] Round and round and round.

144
00:06:26,466 --> 00:06:31,566
It's called a lighthouse
because it has this big light at the top.

145
00:06:32,099 --> 00:06:33,333
[children] Wow!

146
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,366
[Grampy Rabbit] It shines through
the dark,

147
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:37,400
helping sailors to find their way.

148
00:06:37,466 --> 00:06:38,366
[children] Ooh.

149
00:06:38,433 --> 00:06:42,099
And when it's foggy, I use this foghorn.

150
00:06:42,566 --> 00:06:45,000
Fog!

151
00:06:45,066 --> 00:06:47,066
That's loud.

152
00:06:47,133 --> 00:06:50,000
No fog today, just sea and sky.

153
00:06:50,666 --> 00:06:52,266
The stories I could tell--

154
00:06:52,333 --> 00:06:54,400
[Granddad Dog] No, thank you.
We've got to go.

155
00:06:54,466 --> 00:06:58,200
[snorts] We're sailing to Pirate Island.

156
00:06:58,266 --> 00:07:00,366
[children] Goodbye, Grampy Rabbit.

157
00:07:00,433 --> 00:07:03,233
Enjoy the sea and the sky!

158
00:07:03,299 --> 00:07:04,433
[children] We will.

159
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,566
[horn toots]

160
00:07:06,233 --> 00:07:09,799
[narrator] Granddad Dog's boat has arrived
at Pirate Island.

161
00:07:10,033 --> 00:07:13,166
Look, our sand castle is still here.

162
00:07:13,233 --> 00:07:15,433
Let's play hide-and-seek.

163
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,500
Okay.

164
00:07:16,566 --> 00:07:18,066
One, two, three...

165
00:07:18,133 --> 00:07:21,500
[narrator] There are not many places
to hide on Pirate Island.

166
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:24,233
Ready or not, here I come.

167
00:07:25,233 --> 00:07:26,566
-[Danny woofs]
-Found you.

168
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:29,400
-[Danny &amp; Peppa] Oh.
-Now, where's George?

169
00:07:29,466 --> 00:07:30,533
[children giggling]

170
00:07:30,599 --> 00:07:33,400
[narrator] Granddad Dog
cannot find George anywhere.

171
00:07:33,466 --> 00:07:36,500
-I give up. Where is he?
-Boo!

172
00:07:36,566 --> 00:07:39,233
[narrator] George was hiding
behind Granddad Dog.

173
00:07:39,299 --> 00:07:41,599
-Clever George.
-[George snorts]

174
00:07:41,666 --> 00:07:45,200
Let's set off home, before it gets dark.

175
00:07:48,166 --> 00:07:50,633
Oh, it is getting dark.

176
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:51,799
Don't worry.

177
00:07:52,033 --> 00:07:56,566
The light from Grampy Rabbit's lighthouse
will show us the way home.

178
00:07:56,633 --> 00:07:59,133
[narrator] Grampy Rabbit is ready for bed.

179
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:03,033
Oh, my new book,
How to Run a Lighthouse.

180
00:08:03,099 --> 00:08:04,566
"Chapter One."

181
00:08:04,633 --> 00:08:06,066
[yawns]

182
00:08:06,133 --> 00:08:08,133
I'll read the rest tomorrow.

183
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,766
Better turn the light out.

184
00:08:10,566 --> 00:08:13,266
[Peppa] Oh, where did the light go?

185
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
[ringing]

186
00:08:18,533 --> 00:08:22,033
Do you know what time it is?
I've turned the lights out.

187
00:08:22,099 --> 00:08:23,733
Yes, we know.

188
00:08:23,799 --> 00:08:26,566
Could you turn the big light on again?

189
00:08:26,633 --> 00:08:28,099
Oh, sorry.

190
00:08:29,633 --> 00:08:31,433
[all] Hooray!

191
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:33,033
[narrator] It is getting foggy.

192
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,733
I can't see the light anymore.

193
00:08:37,199 --> 00:08:38,466
It's us again.

194
00:08:38,533 --> 00:08:40,633
Could you sound the foghorn?

195
00:08:40,699 --> 00:08:42,033
[Grampy Rabbit] Of course.

196
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,633
Fog!

197
00:08:44,699 --> 00:08:47,166
-I can hear something.
-[Grampy Rabbit] Fog!

198
00:08:47,233 --> 00:08:49,533
[narrator] Grampy Rabbit
is guiding them home.

199
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:54,166
-His voice is a foghorn.
-[Grampy Rabbit] This way! This way home!

200
00:08:55,033 --> 00:08:57,633
[narrator] The parents are here
to pick up the children.

201
00:08:57,699 --> 00:09:01,533
-Have you had a lovely time?
-We went to Pirate Island.

202
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,466
And to a lighthouse.

203
00:09:03,533 --> 00:09:06,733
Grampy Rabbit's lighthouse
guided us home safely.

204
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:08,000
That's nice.

205
00:09:08,066 --> 00:09:11,000
Grampy Rabbit sang a song.

206
00:09:11,066 --> 00:09:12,666
Would you like to hear it?

207
00:09:12,733 --> 00:09:15,199
-No, thanks.
-[parents] Yes, please.

208
00:09:15,266 --> 00:09:16,766
♪ I got up this morning ♪

209
00:09:17,566 --> 00:09:19,533
♪ The sea was still there ♪

210
00:09:20,133 --> 00:09:22,100
♪ So was the sky ♪

211
00:09:23,033 --> 00:09:25,233
♪ The sea, the sky, the sea, the sky ♪

212
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:28,533
♪ The sea, the sky, the sea, the sky ♪

213
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,600
[children giggling]

